※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4615 LANG_ARENA_VALUE_GIVEN_BACK

※ A name read after its arena was given back is one mistake, said once.  Answering it from
※ the function that made the arena would be refused too (4613), but that is the same value
※ going somewhere after it was already gone, and saying so again would be two messages for
※ one line that is wrong for one reason.

fn f(first: str) → str:
    let scratch: mut arena = ⎕arena
    let both: str = first ⧺ "<-" in scratch
    ⎕empty(scratch)
    both

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    if f("a") = "a<-": 0u6 else: 1u6
